-- title:
--   Constant-term retraction on the ∞-chart algebra, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$ and $M'$ a non-zero level with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ belongs to the non-units of $A$. Two function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion of the first in the second. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ is given, with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places $w$ that are rational (the residue field of $w$ is generated by the base field), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-coordinate `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. Further data: a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue map onto the characteristic-$q$ field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with a place map preserving degrees and orders; the hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally, a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`), a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa-chart hypotheses are four. `hIg_inf` identifies the ring at the point `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$ as a Gauss ring: $f$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ non-zero and $f\cdot y = x$ after coefficientwise inclusion of $A$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. `hIg` requires, for each point $\ell$ of the projective line, some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries $[1:0]$ to $\ell$ and with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. `hIg_inj` states that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective, and `hIg_perm` that for every primitive root $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the operation of taking preimages along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ through some permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line.
--
--   The supersingular-chart hypotheses are four. `hSS_A` says that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ lies over $A$: a constant from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` relates $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ to $R_0$: for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular wherever the $j$-expansion is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, non-negativity of the order at $P$ of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image of `jq` forces non-negativity of the order of $f$ at $P$), if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix` states that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under preimage along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a \in A$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$.
--
--   In addition: a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` whose ring of integers is $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ (`hR`), and `hR₀O` saying that $f$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$; an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`); an auxiliary prime $\ell \geq 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ carrying a valuation subring $A_1$ whose elements are exactly those of $K_1$ lying in $A$, $A_1$ being a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the algebra structure of $k_0$ on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of $k_0$ in `fieldBar q M'` subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the whole image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all primitive roots $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ finite over $k_0$, every finite family $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, a relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, i.e. has coefficients in $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum, inside `fieldBar q M'`, of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. For any $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ compatible with the inclusions (the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{A_1\to T_1}(a)$ is the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`), and for any $j_1 \in T_1$ with $j_1 \neq 0$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image of the $j$-expansion `jq`, there exists a ring homomorphism
--   $$\psi : \mathrm{chartAlgInf}(A_1, T_1, j_1) \longrightarrow A_1,$$
--   where [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144) is the subalgebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, such that all of the following hold: $\psi$ is a retraction of the structure map, i.e. $\psi(\mathrm{algebraMap}_{A_1\to\cdot}(a)) = a$ for all $a \in A_1$; $\psi$ annihilates the distinguished element `jInvChartInf`, that is $\psi(j_1^{-1}) = 0$; every $b$ in the chart algebra, viewed in `fieldBar q M'`, lies in `qIntegersBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, i.e. its Laurent series has non-negative order; for every such $b$ the coefficient in degree $0$ of its Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equals the image of $\psi(b) \in A_1 \subseteq K_1$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and, for every $b$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, the value $\psi(b)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A_1$.
--
--   This is the cusp section, or constant-term homomorphism, on the $\infty$-chart of the two-chart integral model of the level field over $A_1$: it produces an $A_1$-point of that model which kills $j_1^{-1}$, reads off the constant term of $q$-expansions, and sends non-units of the Gauss ring at the $\infty$-Igusa component into the maximal ideal of $A_1$. It is the case $q = 3$ of the statement, and is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_centred_of_toValuationSubring_eq_qIntegersBar_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_centred_of_toValuationSubring_eq_qIntegersBar_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three) to centre a place of the level field at the resulting point of the special fibre.
